    "q-127645": {
      "dom_id": "step-q127645",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $P(3,-2,4)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨1,-2,-1⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨3,-2,4⟩,$ and $n=⟨1,-2,-1⟩$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-p)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,-1⟩ & =⟨3,-2,4⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-2,-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-2,-1⟩ & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
