    "q-33035": {
      "dom_id": "step-q33035",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point  $P(1,-\\sqrt{3},4)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=8i+\\sqrt{27}j.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=i-\\sqrt{3}j+4k$ and $n=8i+\\sqrt{27}j$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes through the point $P({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as \n\n$$\n(r-p)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot (8i+\\sqrt{27}j) & =(i-\\sqrt{3}j+4k)\\cdot (8i+\\sqrt{27}j) \\\\ r\\cdot (8i+\\sqrt{27}j) & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
