    "q-32972": {
      "dom_id": "step-q32972",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $Q(5,-1,1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨-1,-2,3⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨5,-1,1⟩$ and $n=⟨-1,-2,3⟩$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $Q({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-q)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,-2,3⟩ & =⟨5,-1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,-2,3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,-2,3⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-32972-a",
