      "kp_id": "e-4935"
    },
    "q-70883": {
      "dom_id": "step-q70883",
      "name": "Question 14",
      "problem": "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(1,2,3)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(2,1,0)$ and $B(1,3,5).$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=⟨1,2,3⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(2,1,0)$ and $B(1,3,5)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨1,3,5⟩-⟨2,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,2,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-1,2,5⟩.$ \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,5⟩ & =⟨1,2,3⟩\\cdot ⟨-1,2,5⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-1,2,5⟩ & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
